      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Select the options that make the statement below true.\n\n$\\,$\n$20%$ is equivalent to \n{{field-1}},\nwhich is \n{{field-2}}\n$\\frac{2}{5}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To convert the percent to a fraction, we first write $20%$ as a fraction with a denominator $100:$\n\n$$\n20%=\\frac{20}{100}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the fraction by dividing the numerator and denominator by $10:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{20}{100}=\\frac{20÷10}{100÷10}=\\frac{2}{10}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{10}=\\frac{2÷2}{10÷2}=\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}<\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $20%$ is equivalent to $\\frac{1}{5},$ \nwhich is $\\text{smaller than}$ $\\frac{2}{5}.$",
